  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday) \nIssued at 816 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nThrough the long term forecast, high pressure looks to build in again\nover the mid Atlantic states and extend back into the TN Valley. This\nwill induce weak SSW flow at the surface and keep humid summer like\nconditions in place each day. Highs looks to remain in the 90s with\ndew points in the high 60s to low 70s. This will push heat indices\nnear and above triple digits each day. While not approaching any \nrecords, these temperatures and dew points will be unseasonably high,\npresenting more like summer than mid September. Please make sure to \ncontinue to practice proper heat and sun safety during our\ncontinued hot and humid conditions. \n\nDue to the higher humidity for mid September, we will have low\nchances for rain and perhaps a stray thunderstorm each afternoon.\nCoverage currently looks very scattered. Without any specific forcing\nmechanism it will be hard to nail down specific times or locations\nthat may have better chances for rain. Please check back for updates\nregarding our low rain chances next week.",
